                  <provenance><orgName role="fmo" key="mlgbOrg_122">Canterbury, Kent. Benedictine
                        abbey of St Augustine (originally of St Peter and St Paul)</orgName><p>Three ex libris inscriptions, two of s. xv on fols. Dv and Er
                        (both sharing the wording of the entry in the Catalogue), with 'fratris
                        Iohannis Bertelot', and the third on fol. 156v. A monk of this name was
                        subdeacon at the abbey in 1356 and priest in 1357.</p><p>'Policronicon ...
                        Cronica plurium temporum fratris Iohannis bertelot. De libraria sancti Aug'
                        Cant' Dist. Xa Gra. III' (f. viv)</p><p>Ancient Libraries, no.
                     932</p></provenance>
                  <provenance type="MLGB3_laterOwners">John Dee (his 'Jupiter' mark on f.
                     vii).</provenance>
                  <provenance type="MLGB3_laterOwners">Belonged to Cornelius Duyn of the Hague in
                     1608 (f. iii).</provenance>
                  <provenance type="MLGB3_laterOwners">Bollandists' MS N 15</provenance>
                  <provenance type="MLGB3_laterOwners">T. James, Ecloga II 80, notes Jo. Bertelot.
                     Polychronicon as no. 170 in Sir Walter Cope's library, evidently this
                     MS.</provenance>
               </history>
